### [2026-05-15T00:00] | lib/theme/colors.dart | MODIFY | COMPLETE REWRITE
- Replaced flat single-value colors with 10-step color scales (50-900) for primary (vibrant violet-indigo), secondary (warm amber-gold), tertiary (rose-pink), emerald, sky blue, orange
- Added separate light/dark surface tokens (canvas, surface, surfaceContainer variants, elevated)
- Added separate light/dark text tokens (ink, inkSecondary, inkMuted)
- Added separate light/dark border tokens
- Added separate light/dark glass effect tokens (background, modal, border)
- Added new gradient presets: gradientPrimary, gradientBrand, gradientWarm, gradientDark, gradientLight, gradientSunset, gradientOcean
### [2026-05-15T00:03] | lib/theme/colors.dart | MODIFY | CONFLICT FIX
- Added back legacy const fields (canvas, surface, surfaceElevated, surfaceOverlay, surfaceHigh, surfaceContainer variants, glassBackground, glassBorder, glassModalBackground, ink, inkSecondary, inkMuted, borderDefault, borderSubtle, outline, outlineVariant) as aliases to light-mode values — zero breakage for 200+ existing references
- Renamed mode-resolved helper methods from canvas()/surface()/etc. to resolveCanvas()/resolveSurface()/etc. to avoid Dart naming conflicts with const fields
- Legacy const fields point to light-mode values (backward compat). Dark mode is handled by Theme.of(context).colorScheme in the theme system, not by these const fields
- Kept ALL legacy aliases (tier, tierColors, achievement colors, status colors, misc) for backward compatibility
- KEY CHANGE: primary changed from dull gray (#5D5F5F) to vibrant violet (#7C3AED)

